      "message": "\u003e I am wondering if this wouldn\u0027t be better to go into common/power_button_x86.c which seems to have a lot of related logic for looking at the charger and interfacing to the chipset API.\n\nI agree, I can move this to that file instead.\n\n\u003e There is already logic to check the battery state in set_pwrbtn_to_pch(), which calls chipset_exit_hardoff().\n\nLogic is indeed included in `set_pwrbtn_to_pch`, but I do not see `chipset_exit_hardoff` being called there, only setting `GPIO_PCH_PWRBTN_L` level.\n\nIn either case, this change prevents moving forward on the state machine if battery is not ready:\n```\n\tcase SYS_POWER_STATE_G3S5:\n\t\tif (!ap_power_is_ok_to_power_up()) {\n\t\t\tap_power_force_shutdown(\n\t\t\t\tAP_POWER_SHUTDOWN_BATTERY_INHIBIT);\n\t\t\treturn SYS_POWER_STATE_G3;\n\t\t}\n```",
